{"id":"mahabharata-2-023","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":23,"title":"त्रयोविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 23 · Arjuna conquers the north: Bhagadatta","summary":{"en":"The four brothers set out to conquer the four quarters. Arjuna goes north, subdues many kingdoms, and after an eight-day battle wins over Bhagadatta of Pragjyotisha, who agrees to pay tribute out of friendship for Pandu's son.","kn":"ನಾಲ್ವರು ಸಹೋದರರು ನಾಲ್ಕು ದಿಕ್ಕುಗಳನ್ನು ಜಯಿಸಲು ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಉತ್ತರಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಅನೇಕ ರಾಜ್ಯಗಳನ್ನು ಜಯಿಸಿ, ಎಂಟು ದಿನದ ಯುದ್ಧದ ನಂತರ ಪ್ರಾಗ್ಜ್ಯೋತಿಷದ ಭಗದತ್ತನನ್ನು ಒಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡುಪುತ್ರನ ಸ್ನೇಹಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಅವನು ಕಪ್ಪ ಕೊಡಲು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"चारों भाई चारों दिशाओं को जीतने निकलते हैं। अर्जुन उत्तर जाकर अनेक राज्यों को वश में करते हैं, और आठ दिन के युद्ध के बाद प्राग्ज्योतिष के भगदत्त को जीत लेते हैं, जो पाण्डुपुत्र की मित्रता के कारण कर देने को मान जाते हैं।","te":"నలుగురు సోదరులు నాలుగు దిక్కులను జయించడానికి బయలుదేరుతారు. అర్జునుడు ఉత్తరానికి వెళ్లి అనేక రాజ్యాలను జయించి, ఎనిమిది రోజుల యుద్ధం తర్వాత ప్రాగ్జ్యోతిష భగదత్తుని గెలుచుకుంటాడు; పాండుపుత్రుని స్నేహం కోసం అతడు కప్పం కట్టడానికి అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"நான்கு சகோதரர்களும் நான்கு திசைகளையும் வெல்லப் புறப்படுகிறார்கள். அர்ஜுனன் வடக்கே சென்று பல நாடுகளை வென்று, எட்டு நாள் போருக்குப் பின் ப்ராக்ஜ்யோதிஷ மன்னன் பகதத்தனை வசப்படுத்துகிறான்; பாண்டுவின் மகன் மீதான நட்பால் அவன் கப்பம் செலுத்த இசைகிறான்.","ml":"നാലു സഹോദരന്മാരും നാലു ദിക്കുകളും കീഴടക്കാൻ പുറപ്പെടുന്നു. അർജുനൻ വടക്കോട്ട് പോയി നിരവധി രാജ്യങ്ങളെ കീഴടക്കുന്നു; എട്ടു ദിവസത്തെ യുദ്ധത്തിനൊടുവിൽ പ്രാഗ്ജ്യോതിഷത്തിലെ ഭഗദത്തനെ കീഴടക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡുവിന്റെ പുത്രനോടുള്ള സൗഹൃദത്താൽ അദ്ദേഹം കപ്പം നൽകാൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.23; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"दिग्विजयपर्व","titleEn":"Digvijaya Parva (Conquest of the quarters)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पार्थः प्राप्य धनुःश्रेष्ठमक्षय्यौ च महेषुधी ।\nरथं ध्वजं सभां चैव युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having obtained the finest bow, the two inexhaustible quivers, a chariot, a banner and the hall, Arjuna spoke to Yudhishthira."}},{"n":2,"text":"धनुरस्त्रं शरा वीर्यं पक्षो भूमिर्यशो बलम् ।\nप्राप्तमेतन्मया राजन्दुष्प्रापं यदभीप्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said: Bow, weapons, arrows, valour, allies, land, fame and strength—all this, hard to win, I have obtained as I wished, O king."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र कृत्यमहं मन्ये कोशस्यास्य विवर्धनम् ।\nकरमाहारयिष्यामि राज्ञः सर्वान्नृपोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the next task is to enlarge the treasury; I will bring tribute from all the kings, best of rulers."}},{"n":4,"text":"विजयाय प्रयास्यामि दिशं धनदरक्षिताम् ।\nतिथावथ मुहूर्ते च नक्षत्रे च तथा शिवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will set out to conquer the direction guarded by Kubera, on an auspicious lunar day, hour and star."}},{"n":5,"text":"धनंजयवचः श्रुत्वा धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nस्निग्धगम्भीरनादिन्या तं गिरा प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Arjuna's words, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, answered him in a voice affectionate and deep."}},{"n":6,"text":"स्वस्ति वाच्यार्हतो विप्रान्प्रयाहि भरतर्षभ ।\nदुर्हृदामप्रहर्षाय सुहृदां नन्दनाय च ।\nविजयस्ते ध्रुवं पार्थ प्रियं काममवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: Have the worthy brahmins pronounce blessings and go, bull of the Bharatas, to dismay your foes and delight your friends. Victory is certain for you, Partha; may you win what you desire."}},{"n":7,"text":"इत्युक्तः प्रययौ पार्थः सैन्येन महता वृतः ।\nअग्निदत्तेन दिव्येन रथेनाद्भुतकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, Arjuna set out surrounded by a great army, on the wondrous divine chariot given by Agni."}},{"n":8,"text":"तथैव भीमसेनोऽपि यमौ च पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nससैन्याः प्रययुः सर्वे धर्मराजाभिपूजिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Bhimasena and the twin sons of Madri, best of men, honoured by Yudhishthira, each marched out with an army."}},{"n":9,"text":"दिशं धनपतेरिष्टामजयत्पाकशासनिः ।\nभीमसेनस्तथा प्राचीं सहदेवस्तु दक्षिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna conquered the direction dear to Kubera, Bhimasena the east, and Sahadeva the south."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रतीचीं नकुलो राजन्दिशं व्यजयदस्त्रवित् ।\nखाण्डवप्रस्थमध्यास्ते धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, expert in weapons, conquered the west, O king, while Yudhishthira stayed at Khandavaprastha."}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"दिशामभिजयं ब्रह्मन्विस्तरेणानुकीर्तय ।\nन हि तृप्यामि पूर्वेषां शृण्वानश्चरितं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, tell me the conquest of the directions in detail; I never tire of hearing the great deeds of my ancestors."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"धनंजयस्य वक्ष्यामि विजयं पूर्वमेव ते ।\nयौगपद्येन पार्थैर्हि विजितेयं वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will first tell you of Arjuna's conquest; the Pandavas won this earth by acting together."}},{"n":13,"text":"पूर्वं कुणिन्दविषये वशे चक्रे महीपतीन् ।\nधनंजयो महाबाहुर्नातितीव्रेण कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"First, in the land of the Kunindas, mighty-armed Arjuna brought the kings under his sway by means that were not too harsh."}},{"n":14,"text":"आनर्तान्कालकूटांश्च कुणिन्दांश्च विजित्य सः ।\nसुमण्डलं पापजितं कृतवाननुसैनिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated the Anartas, the Kalakutas and the Kunindas, he set Sumandala, who had conquered Papa, over his own troops."}},{"n":15,"text":"स तेन सहितो राजन्सव्यसाची परंतपः ।\nविजिग्ये सकलं द्वीपं प्रतिविन्ध्यं च पार्थिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With him, O king, Savyasachin the scourge of foes conquered the whole island and the king Prativindhya."}},{"n":16,"text":"सकलद्वीपवासांश्च सप्तद्वीपे च ये नृपाः ।\nअर्जुनस्य च सैन्यानां विग्रहस्तुमुलोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fierce clash arose between Arjuna's forces and the kings living on the whole island and across the seven islands."}},{"n":17,"text":"स तानपि महेष्वासो विजित्य भरतर्षभ ।\nतैरेव सहितः सर्वैः प्राग्ज्योतिषमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer defeated them too, bull of the Bharatas, and with all of them together advanced on Pragjyotisha."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्र राजा महानासीद्भगदत्तो विशां पते ।\nतेनासीत्सुमहद्युद्धं पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the great king Bhagadatta ruled, lord of men, and he fought a huge battle with the high-souled Pandava."}},{"n":19,"text":"स किरातैश्च चीनैश्च वृतः प्राग्ज्योतिषोऽभवत् ।\nअन्यैश्च बहुभिर्योधैः सागरानूपवासिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by Kiratas, Chinas and many other warriors dwelling by the sea and in marshy lands, he held Pragjyotisha."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः स दिवसानष्टौ योधयित्वा धनंजयम् ।\nप्रहसन्नब्रवीद्राजा संग्रामे विगतक्लमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After fighting Arjuna for eight days, the king, unwearied in battle, said to him with a laugh:"}},{"n":21,"text":"उपपन्नं महाबाहो त्वयि पाण्डवनन्दन ।\nपाकशासनदायादे वीर्यमाहवशोभिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta said: Such valour befits you, mighty-armed joy of the Pandavas, heir of Indra, who shines in battle."}},{"n":22,"text":"अहं सखा सुरेन्द्रस्य शक्रादनवमो रणे ।\nन च शक्नोमि ते तात स्थातुं प्रमुखतो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am a friend of Indra and in battle not inferior to Shakra, yet I cannot stand before you in combat."}},{"n":23,"text":"किमीप्सितं पाण्डवेय ब्रूहि किं करवाणि ते ।\nयद्वक्ष्यसि महाबाहो तत्करिष्यामि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me what you wish, Pandava; what shall I do for you? Whatever you say, child, I will do."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"कुरूणामृषभो राजा धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nतस्य पार्थिवतामीप्से करस्तस्मै प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, is the bull among the Kurus. I wish him to be a sovereign; let tribute be given to him."}},{"n":25,"text":"भवान्पितृसखा चैव प्रीयमाणो मयापि च ।\nततो नाज्ञापयामि त्वां प्रीतिपूर्वं प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are my father's friend and I am pleased with you, so I do not command you; give it out of affection."}},{"text":"भगदत्त उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"कुन्तीमातर्यथा मे त्वं तथा राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nसर्वमेतत्करिष्यामि किं चान्यत्करवाणि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira is to me what you are, a son of Kunti. I will do all this; what else can I do for you?"}}]}]}